      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The fact that the pattern of blood enzymes (CPK, MB CPK, GOT, LDG, LDG-1 and LDG-2) and ratios thereof (CPK/GOT, CPK/LDG, LDG-1/LDG-2) is similar in acute unstable angina to that of myocardial infarction is suggestive of possible myocardial involvement, which is however associated with a smaller ischemic focus."},
